meta {
  name: RTMP conns
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{relayApi}}/v3/rtmpconns/list
  body: none
  auth: none
}

tests {
  test("answers a list, or 404 where the listener is off", function () {
    if (res.getStatus() === 404) {
      return;
    }
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
    expect(res.body.items).to.be.an("array");
  });
}

docs {
  # RTMP conns

  The RTMP connections, with the bytes sent and the frames the relay dropped rather than fall behind.

  Discarded frames are the one congestion signal a protocol with no round trip and no loss rate still gives, and they are a fact about the relay rather than about the line.
}
